#Agile testing pyramid

            What:
            Agile Testing Pyramid is a model that suggests having more tests at lower levels and fewer tests at higher levels.

            Levels:

                    UI / E2E Tests
                ───────────────
                    API / Service
                ─────────────────
                Unit Tests
                ─────────────────────

            From bottom → top:

            Unit Tests: Most, fast and stable
            API/Service Tests: Moderate
            UI/E2E Tests: Fewer, slower and more expensive

            Purpose:

            Faster feedback
            Reduce test execution time
            Lower maintenance cost
            Catch defects as early as possible

            QA Role:
            QA/SDET focuses on maintaining a good balance of API, UI, and automation coverage, rather than relying only on UI tests.

            Interview Answer:

            "The Agile Testing Pyramid recommends having a larger number of fast and reliable unit tests, a moderate number of API or service-level tests, and fewer UI or end-to-end tests. This provides faster feedback and reduces test execution and maintenance costs."